{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-af4812a1094ff804","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# AI Signal Rationale — RHAISTRAT-8010-E002 (Implementation)\n2\t\n3\tManager-binary reconciliation error log standardization (5 controller tiers, 15 action files).\n4\t\n5\t| Signal | Value | Rationale |\n6\t|--------|-------|-----------|\n7\t| change_specificity | 1 | The strategy names the exact controllers, action-file paths (`components/<name>/<name>_controller_actions.go`, `services/{auth,gateway,monitoring}/*_controller_actions.go`, `datasciencecluster/datasciencecluster_controller_actions.go`, `modules/modules_controller_actions*.go`), field names (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`), and before/after call shapes. |\n8\t| pattern_precedent | 1 | Structured-field logging already exists in the same codebase: framework controllers emit `name`/`namespace` via controller-runtime's request logger, and `modules_controller_actions_inject_env.go` already uses structured fields — the conversion follows an in-repo pattern. |\n9\t| adapter_pattern | 0 | No adapter/plugin pattern is involved; this is a uniform mechanical edit to log call sites. |\n10\t| existing_foundation | 1 | Pure extension of existing code: controller-runtime/logr infrastructure is used throughout rhods-operator (confirmed by architecture context), and no new logging framework is introduced. |\n11\t| open_questions | 1 | All design decisions for this epic are resolved (fields, naming convention, target files). The remaining open questions — the audit percentage and the alert-rule inventory — change effort, not approach, and the convention-field question concerns optional extensions beyond this epic's HLR-mandated fields. |\n12\t| external_dependency | 1 | None: the only dependency (controller-runtime logr) is internal and confirmed to exist; no upstream contribution or vendor coordination is needed for the manager work. |\n13\t| human_process_gates | -1 | The strategy