int exception into E004).\n56\t\n57\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n58\tAll strategy scope is accounted for: manager binary (all 5 controller tiers, 15 action files, DSCI migration) → E002; cloudmanager (3 controllers, shared-reconciler specifics, \"if applicable\" non-standard keys) → E003; CI lint/static-analysis measurement → E004; contribution guideline, publication, and external-operator outreach → E005. Every strategy acceptance criterion maps to an epic AC, including the cluster-scoped resource case and the single-release DSCI transition. Strategy-level context is carried forward, not dropped: all four risks appear as epic scope/ACs or the E002 Risks section; all four open questions are explicitly handled (E001 investigation, ACs on E002/E003, E003 release-phasing note plus a health warning); the backwards-compatibility NFR's verification method is an AC on both implementation epics; the performance NFR requires no verification per the strategy. The design-doc elements listed in Supporting Documentation (three-problem diagnosis, before/after examples, DSCI migration guide) are covered by E005's guideline scope. External COO adoption is correctly not modeled as an epic per platform policy overlay 0008, with best-effort tracking issues in E005. Documentation Support is listed in the strategy's prerequisites and a docs-authoring epic exists.\n59\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-98bf105a555a0a8e","agent_id":"abd5d2cf9a21bd40f","session_id":"91ced742-efea-4af7-ba7b-29299f310824","uuid":"d52cb7c6-7ecb-4c0a-bc7a-edaa4b47eb34","timestamp":"2026-10-21T18:03:03.594Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b4ef00ffaa416bc7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8010 decomposition"}
