{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b36030098ea79129","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8010-E001\n3\ttitle: Resolve structured log field convention scope (fields beyond name/namespace/resourceKind)\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8010\n5\tcomponent: OpenShift AI Productization\n6\tteam: ODH Operator team\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 0\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -2\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Low\n19\tai_implementability_score: -1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Resolve structured log field convention scope (fields beyond name/namespace/resourceKind)\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis investigation resolves the strategy's open product question: whether the rhods-operator structured log field convention should include fields beyond the three required ones (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`). Candidate additions raised in the strategy are reconciliation attempt count and error category. The decision determines the final content of the contribution guideline that documents the convention for new controller development and for voluntary adoption by external operator teams, and whether any optional fields are recommended. The question is owned by the ODH Operator team with PM / Observability team input, per the strategy's open-question ownership.\n30\t\n31\tThe required fields themselves are fixed by the strategy's P0 requirements and are not in question; only optional extensions to the convention are decided here.\n32\t\n33\t## Scope\n34\t\n35\t- Enumerate candidate additional structured fields (e.g., reconciliation attempt count, error category) and evaluate each against the stated tradeoff: additional utility versus increased log volume\n36\t- Decide, with PM / Observability team input, whether the convention is limited to the three required fields or extended with optional/recommended fields\n37\t- Record the decision and its rationale as a decision record, specifying the final convention field set (required fields, optional fields if any, or explicitly none)\n38\t- If additional fields are adopted, identify the follow-up implementation work needed to emit them, so it can be planned\n39\t\n40\t## Acceptance Criteria\n41\t\n42\t- Given the candidate additional fields, when the decision is made, then the convention's complete field set is explicitly enumerated (required vs. optional vs. none), with rationale for the inclusion or exclusion of each candidate\n43\t- The decision explicitly accounts for the log-volume impact of any adopted additional fields\n44\t- The decision record is published to the stakeholders of the convention documentation work so the contribution guideline can be authored against the resolved field set\n45\t- If additional fields are adopted, the follow-up implementation impact on the already-standardized reconciliation error logs is identified and documented\n46\t\n47\t## HLR Traceability\n48\t\n49\t- Supports the P1 HLR \"Document the convention as a contribution guideline for new controller development and publish for external operator adoption\" — this investigation resolves the open question that gates the guideline's content (which fields the convention specifies)\n50\t- No HLR is directly implemented by this epic; the P0 required fields (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`) are implemented by the manager and cloudmanager standardization work independently of this decision\n51\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8841b43c5f8a16cd","agent_id":"a4812aff32f2b2d36","session_id":"91ced742-efea-4af7-ba7b-29299f310824","uuid":"42a10db8-4a58-4b7e-9080-b1a61127888e","timestamp":"2026-10-21T18:06:22.933Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b36030098ea79129","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8010 decomposition"}
