{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b0d3e50aac548c4c","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8010-E002\n3\ttitle: Standardize reconciliation error logs across the rhods-operator manager binary\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8010\n5\tcomponent: OpenShift AI Productization\n6\tteam: ODH Operator team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: -1\n18\t  repo_access: 0\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 5\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Standardize reconciliation error logs across the rhods-operator manager binary\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic converts all reconciliation error logs in the rhods-operator manager binary to the structured logging convention: resource name and namespace emitted as structured key-value pairs instead of being embedded in message strings, `resourceKind` added as a structured field to every controller and action-file error log, and the DSCInitialization (DSCI) controller migrated off its non-standard key names. The work spans all five controller tiers of the manager binary — the DataScienceCluster (DSC) controller, the 8 component controllers (DataSciencePipelines, Kueue, ModelRegistry, Ray, SparkOperator, Trainer, TrainingOperator, TrustyAI), the module controller with its 8 module handlers (Dashboard, AIGateway, KServe, OGX, Workbenches, MLflowOperator, FeastOperator, MCPLifecycleOperator), the DSCI controller, and the 5 service controllers (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator, Setup) — plus all 15 action files across the four tiers (8 component action files under `components/<name>/<name>_controller_actions.go`, 3 service action files under `services/{auth,gateway,monitoring}/*_controller_actions.go`, 1 DSC action file under `datasciencecluster/datasciencecluster_controller_actions.go`, and 3 module action files under `modules/modules_controller_actions*.go`).\n34\t\n35\tThe logging infrastructure (controller-runtime logr) already exists, and the framework controllers (DSC and the 8 component controllers) already emit `name` and `namespace` via controller-runtime's request logger at the reconcile entry point; the missing pieces are the field conversions, the `resourceKind` field, and the DSCI key-name migration.\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\t- Audit all `log.Error()` call sites in reconciliation error paths across the manager binary's controllers and action files, using grep/static analysis, and track coverage in a checklist (the strategy's 75% embedded-identity figure is an estimate to be confirmed by this audit)\n40\t- For each call site embedding resource name or namespace in the message string, extract the identity fields and convert to structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`), leaving the log message as a stable, identity-free string\n41\t- Add `resourceKind` as a structured field to all reconciliation error logs:\n42\t  - Service controllers, module controller (all 8 module handlers), DSCI controller, and all 15 action files — required (P0), because the reconciled kind is not implied by the controller name for these\n43\t  - DSC and the 8 component controllers — queryability enhancement (P1), included here because it edits the same call sites as the identity conversion. This P1 sub-scope is separable for planning: it can be deferred or cut from this epic without affecting any of the P0 scope above, so planners can drop the queryability enhancement independently of the P0 conversion work\n44\t- Migrate the DSCI controller's structured field names from the non-standard `Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization` to the camelCase convention (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`), completing the transition in a single release\n45\t- Handle cluster-scoped resources (e.g., DataScienceCluster, DSCInitialization): emit `name` and `resourceKind`, with `namespace` omitted or set to empty string — never a spurious namespace value\n46\t- Add unit tests asserting field presence and correctness by parsing test logger output, per controller tier and across all 15 action files\n47\t- Log consumer regression validation per the backwards-compatibility NFR: before/after log output comparison for a sample reconciliation error; deploy a test build to a dev cluster with the production log consumer stack configured, trigger reconciliation errors, and verify ingestion without configuration changes\n48\t- Coordinate with SRE/Support to identify and update any text-based alert rules that rely on message-string patterns. The DSCI key-migration release-notes documentation (with before/after query examples) is not authored here — it is owned by the convention documentation workstream (the docs-authoring epic for this strategy); this epic supplies the before/after log-output facts that guide needs\n49\t\n50\t## Acceptance Criteria\n51\t\n52\t- Given a manager-binary reconciliation error log call that previously embedded resource name or namespace in the message string, when the code is updated, then the call uses structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`) instead, measured by static analysis or CI lint flagging zero remaining `log.Error` calls with identity embedded in message text\n53\t- Given the DSCI controller's reconciliation error logs, when the code is updated, then all structured field names use the camelCase convention (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`) instead of `Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization`, measured by a unit test asserting the standard field names and a codebase grep confirming no references to the old field names remain\n54\t- Given a service controller (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator, Setup) encounters a reconciliation error, when the error is logged, then the entry includes `resourceKind` as a structured field, measured by a unit test parsing test logger output and asserting `resourceKind` is present with the correct value\n55\t- Given an action-file error log in any of the 4 tiers (8 component, 3 service, 1 DSC, 3 module), when the code is updated, then the entry includes `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` as structured fields, measured by unit tests asserting all three fields with correct values across all 15 action files\n56\t- Given the module controller reconciles any of its 8 module handlers and encounters an error, when the error is logged, then the entry includes `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind`, measured by unit test\n57\t- Given DSC and component controller reconciliation errors, when logged, then the entries include `resourceKind`, measured by unit test (cross-controller queryability; P1 enhancement — separable from the P0 acceptance criteria above and deferrable without impacting them)\n58\t- Given a cluster-scoped resource (e.g., DataScienceCluster, DSCInitialization) is reconciled and encounters an error, when the error is logged, then the entry includes `name` and `resourceKind` and `namespace` is omitted or empty, measured by unit test confirming no spurious namespace value\n59\t- Given the log format changes, when a test build runs in a dev cluster with the production log consumer stack, then structured fields appear and consumers (Loki, CloudWatch) ingest both formats without configuration changes, and text-based alert rules identified with SRE/Support have been updated\n60\t- The DSCI key-name migration ships within a single release, avoiding long-term inconsistency between old and new field names\n61\t- All changes pass the repository's structured-log CI check once it is available (coordination, not a blocking dependency)\n62\t\n63\t## HLR Traceability\n64\t\n65\t- [P0] All rhods-operator reconciliation error logs that embed resource name or namespace in message strings are converted to structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`) — manager-binary portion\n66\t- [P0] DSCI controller migrated from non-standard key names (`Request.Name`, `DSCInitialization`) to camelCase convention\n67\t- [P0] All service controller reconciliation error logs include `resourceKind`\n68\t- [P0] All action file error logs include `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` across all 4 tiers (15 action files)\n69\t- [P0] Module controller error logs include `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` (8 module handlers)\n70\t- [P1] DSC and component controller reconciliation error logs include `resourceKind` (bundled here — same call sites as the P0 conversion work; deferring it would duplicate edits to identical log calls. The P1 sub-scope is marked separable in Scope so planners can cut it independently of the P0 work)\n71\t\n72\t## Risks (from strategy)\n73\t\n74\t- Missed error paths during the audit, especially in the action files — mitigated by grep/static-analysis call-site inventory, a coverage checklist, and the CI lint rule\n75\t- Log consumer regression / broken text-based alerts — mitigated by the dev-cluster validation and SRE/Support coordination above\n76\t- Existing Loki/CloudWatch queries filtering on the old DSCI field names — mitigated by the DSCI migration guide (release-notes documentation with before/after query examples, owned by the convention documentation workstream rather than this epic) and a single-release transition\n77\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8841b43c5f8a16cd","agent_id":"a4812aff32f2b2d36","session_id":"91ced742-efea-4af7-ba7b-29299f310824","uuid":"27773691-c8c3-4f76-91a8-84f94a1637a3","timestamp":"2026-10-21T18:06:23.905Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b0d3e50aac548c4c","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8010 decomposition"}
