{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bc49e2ac14aa5d2d","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8010-E004\n3\ttitle: CI lint rule enforcing structured log fields in reconciliation error paths\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8010\n5\tcomponent: OpenShift AI Productization\n6\tteam: ODH Operator team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 0\n15\t  open_questions: 0\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: -1\n18\t  repo_access: 0\n19\t  architecture_claims: 0\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: Medium\n23\tai_implementability_score: 1\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# CI lint rule enforcing structured log fields in reconciliation error paths\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic adds a CI lint rule / static-analysis check to the rhods-operator repository that flags `log.Error()` calls in reconciliation error paths which embed resource name or namespace in the message text or are missing the required structured fields. It is the enforcement and measurement mechanism for the structured log convention: it prevents regression of the converted call sites and enforces the convention for new controller development, which is also a risk mitigation for inconsistent adoption across the many controllers and action files.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Implement a lint rule or static-analysis check (mechanism choice — linter integration vs. standalone analysis script — is an implementation decision for the team) that flags `log.Error()` calls which:\n38\t  - embed resource name or namespace in the message string, or\n39\t  - lack the required structured fields (`name`, `namespace` where the resource is namespaced, `resourceKind`)\n40\t- Correctly handle cluster-scoped resources: a missing or empty `namespace` must not be falsely flagged\n41\t- Wire the check into the repository's CI so that new violations fail the build\n42\t- Scope the check to reconciliation error paths per the strategy (non-reconciliation log paths are explicitly out of scope)\n43\t- Document how developers run the check locally and remediate flagged calls\n44\t\n45\t## Acceptance Criteria\n46\t\n47\t- Given a `log.Error` call that embeds resource name or namespace in the message string, when CI runs on a pull request, then the check flags it — this is the \"measured by\" clause of the strategy's primary acceptance criterion\n48\t- Given a reconciliation error log call missing required structured fields, when CI runs, then the check flags it\n49\t- Given a conforming call site (structured KV pairs present, identity-free message), when CI runs, then the check passes it\n50\t- Given a cluster-scoped resource error log with `namespace` omitted or empty, when CI runs, then the check does not flag it as a violation\n51\t- The check runs automatically in CI on every pull request and blocks merge on violation\n52\t- The repository's existing documentation explains how to run the check locally and fix flagged calls\n53\t\n54\t## HLR Traceability\n55\t\n56\t- Supports the [P0] HLR \"All rhods-operator reconciliation error logs that embed resource name or namespace in message strings are converted to structured key-value pairs\" — this epic provides the CI lint / static-analysis measurement and regression prevention for that requirement across both the manager and cloudmanager binaries\n57\t- Implements the risk mitigation \"add a CI lint rule to flag new `log.Error` calls missing required structured fields\" and part of the effort item \"document convention and add CI lint rule\"\n58\t\n59\t## Notes\n60\t\n61\t- This work is developed in parallel with the manager-binary and cloudmanager-binary log standardization; their acceptance criteria include passing this check once available, which is a coordination point, not a sequencing dependency.\n62\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8841b43c5f8a16cd","agent_id":"a4812aff32f2b2d36","session_id":"91ced742-efea-4af7-ba7b-29299f310824","uuid":"1adee35d-30a2-4adc-a928-8d31c736958f","timestamp":"2026-10-21T18:06:28.649Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bc49e2ac14aa5d2d","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8010 decomposition"}
